<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n87141" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προεθ-ίζω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>train beforehand,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡμᾶς ἐπὶ τὰ μείζονα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.531a
				</span></i>
			:—
				Pass.
			, <i>to be so trained,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1337a20
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰς ὃ δεῖ ἐλθεῖν προειθισμένοι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyr.</u>
					6.2.29
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>accustom beforehand,</i> c. dat., <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.256
			</span></i>:—
				Pass.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.223
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> intr.,
				<i>become accustomed,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινι</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				6.36
			</span></i>. <i><span class="en">
				4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ μὴ -είθισται ταῦτα</span> if these
			things <i>have</i> not <i>been settled beforehand by custom,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Simp.
				<u>in Epict.</u>
				p.110D.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
